In this implementation, we negate the values before inserting them into the heap to achieve a max heap behavior. The `insert` function uses `heappush` to insert the negated value into the heap.

The `deleteMax` function uses `heappop` to remove and return the maximum element from the heap. Since the values are negated, we negate the result before returning it.

The `getMax` function returns the maximum element in the heap, which is the negation of the first element in the `heap` list.

The time complexity of the `insert` and `deleteMax` operations is O(log n) since they both rely on the `heappush` and `heappop` functions, which have a time complexity of O(log n) for a heap of size n. The `getMax` operation has a time complexity of O(1) since it only accesses the first element of the `heap` list.

